Answer: According to medical evidence, there is no difference based on mask type, as health experts uniformly state that wearing any face mask does not put you at risk of developing pleurisy. As one pulmonologist dismissed the underlying claim as "complete nonsense," confirming there is "no indication that a face mask carries any health risk whatsoever."

